Add the TX_BLOCK generic parameter (id 6) to morse_cli.

`MORSE_CMD_PARAM_ID_TX_BLOCK = 6` is already declared in the vendor's own
`morse_commands.h`, and both the driver and the firmware accept it with no
association, no vif and no AID: `command.c:1671` switches only on
AP_POWER_SAVE / NON_TIM_MODE / HOME_CHANNEL_DWELL / ACTIVE_SCAN_DWELL /
CHANNELIZATION, so id 6 falls through to `default:` -> `morse_cmd_tx()`, and
firmware handler 0x00132eb4 does `snez` then `sb a5, 0x802006FE` (any non-zero
blocks, no range check, always returns 0). Only `params.c`'s `params[]` table
was missing an entry, so the gate was unreachable from userspace.

MEASURED on an MM6108 (mds-o5p-2, 904.5 MHz / 1 MHz, monitor injection, no
association), chip MAC-core `TX Total` as the instrument (idle drift +0/6 s):

  tx_block=0, inject 200 @100 f/s -> TX Total +200 ; peer received 293/300
  tx_block=1, inject 200          -> TX Total +0   ; peer received 0 in 15 s
  tx_block=0, inject NOTHING      -> TX Total +200 ; peer received 244 in ONE
                                                     1-second bucket
  tx_block=0, inject 200          -> TX Total +200

i.e. it gates, it HOLDS rather than drops, and it is reversible.

Build:
  sed -i 's/ -Werror//' Makefile
  nix-shell -p gcc gnumake pkg-config libnl libusb1 --run \
    'make CONFIG_MORSE_TRANS_NL80211=1 CFLAGS="$(pkg-config --cflags libnl-genl-3.0)" all'

Consumed by `MorseKnobs`'s `RadioKnobs::set_tx_hold` (src/morse.rs). A stock
morse_cli prints "Invalid parameter: 'tx_block'" and exits 1; that path is
reported as an error there, never as a hold that took.

